OpenAdapt quickstart: show a task once, run it, then watch it catch a save that didn't happen.
Synthetic data only. Files go to openadapt-quickstart

1  Show it once · a demonstration in a synthetic clinic app, in a hidden browser
   ✓ Click Open                               0.4s
   ✓ Click New Encounter                      0.7s
   ✓ Click Triage                             0.9s
   ✓ Click Note                               1.1s
   ✓ Type "Synthetic follow-up in two weeks"  1.3s
   ✓ Click Save Encounter                     1.6s
   Compiled into a program: 6 steps. 0.5s

2  Run it · the program on 5 new notes, all at once
   1/5  Follow-up in two weeks             ✓ checked in the database  2.6s
   2/5  Recheck blood pressure next month  ✓ checked in the database  2.7s
   3/5  Refer to physical therapy          ✓ checked in the database  2.8s
   4/5  Repeat labs before next visit      ✓ checked in the database  2.9s
   5/5  No change to the care plan         ✓ checked in the database  3.0s
   5 of 5 saved and checked · 0 AI calls · $0.00 · 0.5s

3  Break it · the next save fails silently
   The app will show its saved message. The database will reject the save.
   What the screen showed:    "Encounter saved — Synthetic follow-up in two weeks"
   What the database showed:  0 new records
   A screen-trusting bot:     ✓ Done
   OpenAdapt:                 ■ Stopped before reporting success  7.7s
   Why: OpenAdapt reads the record back from the database after each save. It found nothing, so it stopped.

The screen said "Encounter saved". The database had nothing. A bot that trusts the screen reports Done. OpenAdapt stopped.

Receipt
  Program    local-quickstart · 6 steps
  Runs       5 of 5 saved and checked in the database
  Cost       0 AI calls · $0.00 · 2.5s in all
  Seal       seal-ed25519-0123456789abcdef · 5 reports signed
See real Seals from OpenEMR runs: https://openadapt.ai/seals
Check it: openadapt seal verify openadapt-quickstart
Details: openadapt-quickstart, one REPORT.md per run; side-by-side page openadapt-quickstart/index.html
Try it on your own app: openadapt flow record --backend web --url https://your-app.example --out my-task
Give your agent this as a tool: openadapt agent serve --allow-run
